  "cites": "the right salt and info with a 64-byte output, the HMAC-SHA256 block size. HKDF's output is not a prefix-free family: the first 32 bytes agree with the 32-byte key, so an implementation that truncates on use interoperates and one that keys HMAC with all 64 bytes does not. The parameter is fixed at 32 bytes so the question never arises.",
